/-!
# Evaluating cohomology classes on fundamental classes

Let `N` be a compact topological `n`-manifold without boundary with an orientation `o`
(`TauCeti.HomologicalOrientation N E n`), and let `f : N → X` be a continuous map to a space `X`.
The fundamental class `[N] ∈ Hₙ(N; ℤ)` pushes forward to a class `f_*[N] ∈ Hₙ(X; ℤ)`, and a
cohomology class `c ∈ Hⁿ(X; M)` with coefficients in an abelian group `M` can be evaluated on it
through the Kronecker map, giving `⟨c, f_*[N]⟩ ∈ M`. For `n = 2` and an embedded closed oriented
surface `f : S → X`, this is the evaluation of a degree-two class on the surface, as in the
Euler-class inequalities for foliations of `3`-manifolds, where `c` is the Euler class of the
tangent plane field.

The pairing is natural: evaluating `c` on the image of `[N]` under `f` is evaluating the pull-back
`f^* c` on `[N]` itself, and for a further map `g : X → Y`, evaluating `c` on `(g ∘ f)_*[N]` is
evaluating `g^* c` on `f_*[N]`. The class `f_*[N]`, and so the pairing, depends only on the
homotopy class of `f`, and reversing the orientation of `N` negates both. For a map `f : N → P` to
a second compact preconnected oriented `n`-manifold, the pairing scales by the degree of `f`:
`⟨f^* c, [N]⟩ = deg f • ⟨c, [P]⟩`.

The pairing is non-degenerate on the manifold itself. If `N` is moreover connected and `M` is an
injective abelian group, such as `ℚ` or `ℚ / ℤ`, then `c ↦ ⟨c, [N]⟩` is a bijection
`Hⁿ(N; M) → M`: the Kronecker map is an isomorphism `Hⁿ(N; M) ≃ Hom(Hₙ(N; ℤ), M)` for injective
coefficients (`TopCat.singularKroneckerEquiv`), and `Hₙ(N; ℤ)` is freely generated by `[N]`
(`TauCeti.HomologicalOrientation.fundamentalClassEquiv`).

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.HomologicalOrientation.evalFundamentalClass`: the `ℤ`-linear evaluation
  `c ↦ ⟨c, f_*[N]⟩` of `Hⁿ(X; M)` on the image
  `TauCeti.HomologicalOrientation.mapFundamentalClass` of the fundamental class under a
  continuous map `f : N → X`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.HomologicalOrientation.evalFundamentalClass_id_singularCohomologyMap`:
  `⟨f^* c, [N]⟩ = ⟨c, f_*[N]⟩`.
* `TauCeti.HomologicalOrientation.evalFundamentalClass_comp`: `⟨c, (g ∘ f)_*[N]⟩ = ⟨g^* c, f_*[N]⟩`.
* `TauCeti.HomologicalOrientation.evalFundamentalClass_singularCohomologyChainCoefficientMap`: for
  a class `v` on chains with coefficients in `ℤ`, the pairing with `f_*[N]` is `⟨f^* v, [N]⟩`
  with `[N]` read in `Hₙ(N; ℤ)`.
* `TauCeti.HomologicalOrientation.evalFundamentalClass_eq_of_homotopic`: homotopic maps give the
  same pairing.
* `TauCeti.HomologicalOrientation.evalFundamentalClass_neg`: reversing the orientation negates the
  pairing.
* `evalFundamentalClass_singularCohomologyChainCoefficientMap_eq_singularKronecker`, in the
  namespace `TauCeti.HomologicalOrientation`: for an integral class with chain coefficients the
  unit `ℤ` of `ModuleCat ℤ`, the pairing is the Kronecker pairing with `f_*[N]` read with chain
  coefficients `ℤ`.
* `TauCeti.HomologicalOrientation.evalFundamentalClass_id_singularCohomologyMap_eq_degree_smul`:
  for a map `f : N → P` of compact oriented `n`-manifolds with `P` preconnected,
  `⟨f^* c, [N]⟩ = deg f • ⟨c, [P]⟩`, and more generally
  `TauCeti.HomologicalOrientation.evalFundamentalClass_comp_eq_degree_smul`:
  `⟨c, (g ∘ f)_*[N]⟩ = deg f • ⟨c, g_*[P]⟩`.
* `TauCeti.HomologicalOrientation.evalFundamentalClass_id_bijective`: for a compact connected
  oriented manifold and injective coefficients, evaluation on the fundamental class is a bijection
  `Hⁿ(N; M) → M`.

## Implementation notes

The manifold `N` and the target space `X` live in `Type`, as for
`TauCeti.HomologicalOrientation.fundamentalClass`, and homology has the integral coefficients
`ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift ℤ)` used there.

## References

* A. Hatcher, [*Algebraic Topology*](https://pi.math.cornell.edu/~hatcher/AT/AT.pdf),
  Section 3.1 (the Kronecker pairing and the universal coefficient theorem) and Section 3.3
  (fundamental classes).
* D. Calegari, *Foliations and the Geometry of 3-Manifolds*, Oxford (2007), Chapter 6 (the Euler
  class of a taut foliation evaluated on surfaces).
-/

public section

noncomputable section

open AlgebraicTopology CategoryTheory Module

namespace TauCeti

namespace HomologicalOrientation

variable {N E : Type} [TopologicalSpace N] [T2Space N]
  [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [ChartedSpace E N]
  [CompactSpace N] {n : ℕ} (o : HomologicalOrientation N E n) (hn : finrank ℝ E = n)
  {X Y : Type} [TopologicalSpace X] [TopologicalSpace Y] (M : ModuleCat.{0} ℤ)

/-- **The evaluation of a cohomology class on the image of a fundamental class**: for a compact
oriented `n`-manifold `N` and a continuous map `f : N → X`, the `ℤ`-linear map
`Hⁿ(X; M) → M`, `c ↦ ⟨c, f_*[N]⟩`, the Kronecker pairing of `c` with
`TauCeti.HomologicalOrientation.mapFundamentalClass`. -/
def evalFundamentalClass (f : C(N, X)) :
    (TopCat.of X).singularCohomology (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) ℤ M n →ₗ[ℤ] M :=
  { toFun c := ((TopCat.of X).singularKronecker (R := ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) (M := M) ℤ n
        c).hom (o.mapFundamentalClass hn f)
    map_add' c d := by simp
    map_smul' a c := by
      simp only [map_smul, ModuleCat.hom_smul, LinearMap.smul_apply, RingHom.id_apply]
      -- The two sides use `zsmul` and the given `ℤ`-module structure of `M`, respectively.
      exact (int_smul_eq_zsmul _ _ _).symm }

/-- The evaluation on `f_*[N]` is the Kronecker map applied to `f_*[N]`. -/
theorem evalFundamentalClass_apply (f : C(N, X))
    (c : (TopCat.of X).singularCohomology (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) ℤ M n) :
    o.evalFundamentalClass hn M f c =
      ((TopCat.of X).singularKronecker ℤ n c).hom (o.mapFundamentalClass hn f) :=
  (rfl)

/-- **Functoriality of the pairing**, `⟨c, (g ∘ f)_*[N]⟩ = ⟨g^* c, f_*[N]⟩`. -/
theorem evalFundamentalClass_comp (g : C(X, Y)) (f : C(N, X))
    (c : (TopCat.of Y).singularCohomology (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) ℤ M n) :
    o.evalFundamentalClass hn M (g.comp f) c =
      o.evalFundamentalClass hn M f (TopCat.singularCohomologyMap (TopCat.ofHom g) n c) := by
  rw [evalFundamentalClass_apply, evalFundamentalClass_apply, mapFundamentalClass_comp,
    TopCat.singularKronecker_naturality]
  -- Both sides are the Kronecker map of `c` applied to `g_* (f_*[N])`; the composite morphism is
  -- applied as a composite of linear maps.
  rfl

/-- **Naturality of the pairing**, `⟨f^* c, [N]⟩ = ⟨c, f_*[N]⟩`: evaluating the pull-back of a
class on the fundamental class is evaluating the class itself on the image of the fundamental
class. -/
@[simp]
theorem evalFundamentalClass_id_singularCohomologyMap (f : C(N, X))
    (c : (TopCat.of X).singularCohomology (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) ℤ M n) :
    o.evalFundamentalClass hn M (ContinuousMap.id N)
        (TopCat.singularCohomologyMap (TopCat.ofHom f) n c) =
      o.evalFundamentalClass hn M f c := by
  simpa using (o.evalFundamentalClass_comp hn M f (ContinuousMap.id N) c).symm

/-- **The pairing for classes on chains with coefficients in `ℤ`.** For a class `v ∈ Hⁿ(X; M)`
built on singular chains with coefficients in `ℤ` rather than `ULift ℤ`, evaluating `v` on
`f_*[N]` after changing the chain coefficients along `ULift ℤ ≅ ℤ` is the Kronecker pairing
`⟨f^* v, [N]⟩` with the fundamental class read in `Hₙ(N; ℤ)` through
`TauCeti.uliftIntHomologyIso`. -/
theorem evalFundamentalClass_singularCohomologyChainCoefficientMap (f : C(N, X))
    (v : (TopCat.of X).singularCohomology (ModuleCat.of ℤ ℤ) ℤ M n) :
    o.evalFundamentalClass hn M f
        ((TopCat.of X).singularCohomologyChainCoefficientMap ℤ M uliftIntIso.hom n v) =
      ((TopCat.of N).singularKronecker ℤ n (TopCat.singularCohomologyMap (TopCat.ofHom f) n v)).hom
        ((uliftIntHomologyIso (TopCat.of N) n).hom.hom (o.fundamentalClass hn)) := by
  symm
  -- term-mode steps: the homology objects are written through `SSet.homology` on one side and
  -- `singularHomologyFunctor` on the other, so `rw` cannot form the motives
  refine (congrArg (fun g ↦ ModuleCat.Hom.hom g
    ((uliftIntHomologyIso (TopCat.of N) n).hom.hom (o.fundamentalClass hn)))
    (TopCat.singularKronecker_naturality (TopCat.ofHom f) ℤ n v)).trans ?_
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (o.evalFundamentalClass_apply hn _ _ _).symm
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (congrArg (fun g ↦ ModuleCat.Hom.hom g (o.mapFundamentalClass hn f))
    (TopCat.singularKronecker_singularCohomologyChainCoefficientMap _ ℤ uliftIntIso.hom n
      v)).symm
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (congrArg (fun g ↦
      (g ≫ (TopCat.of X).singularKronecker ℤ n v).hom (o.mapFundamentalClass hn f))
    (uliftIntHomologyIso_hom (TopCat.of X) n))
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (congrArg (fun x ↦ ModuleCat.Hom.hom
    ((uliftIntHomologyIso (TopCat.of X) n).hom ≫ (TopCat.of X).singularKronecker ℤ n v) x)
    (o.mapFundamentalClass_def hn f)).symm
  exact (congrArg (fun g ↦ (g ≫ (TopCat.of X).singularKronecker ℤ n v).hom
    (o.fundamentalClass hn)) (homologyMap_comp_uliftIntHomologyIso_hom (TopCat.ofHom f) n)).symm

/-- **Homotopy invariance of the pairing**: homotopic maps give the same evaluation. -/
theorem evalFundamentalClass_eq_of_homotopic {f g : C(N, X)} (h : f.Homotopic g) :
    o.evalFundamentalClass hn M f = o.evalFundamentalClass hn M g := by
  ext c
  rw [evalFundamentalClass_apply, evalFundamentalClass_apply,
    o.mapFundamentalClass_eq_of_homotopic hn h]

/-- Reversing the orientation negates the pairing. -/
@[simp]
theorem evalFundamentalClass_neg (f : C(N, X)) :
    (-o).evalFundamentalClass hn M f = -o.evalFundamentalClass hn M f := by
  ext c
  rw [evalFundamentalClass_apply, LinearMap.neg_apply, evalFundamentalClass_apply,
    mapFundamentalClass_neg, map_neg]

/-- **Evaluation on the fundamental class is an isomorphism for injective coefficients.** For a
compact connected oriented `n`-manifold `N` and an injective abelian group `M`, such as `ℚ`, the
map `Hⁿ(N; M) → M`, `c ↦ ⟨c, [N]⟩`, is bijective. -/
theorem evalFundamentalClass_id_bijective [ConnectedSpace N] [CategoryTheory.Injective M] :
    Function.Bijective (o.evalFundamentalClass hn M (ContinuousMap.id N)) := by
  -- Evaluation at `[N]` is evaluation at `1` after transport along `ℤ ≃ Hₙ(N; ℤ)`, `1 ↦ [N]`.
  -- The ascription reads the target of `fundamentalClassEquiv` as the source of the Kronecker map.
  let e : ℤ ≃ₗ[ℤ]
      ((singularHomologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{0} ℤ) n).obj (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ))).obj
        (TopCat.of N) :=
    o.fundamentalClassEquiv hn
  have he : e 1 = o.mapFundamentalClass hn (ContinuousMap.id N) :=
    ((o.fundamentalClassEquiv_apply hn 1).trans (one_smul ℤ _)).trans
      (o.mapFundamentalClass_id hn).symm
  -- Evaluation at `1` is taken `ℕ`-linearly: `M` carries its own `ℤ`-module structure rather
  -- than `zsmul`, so the commuting `ℤ`-actions that `ℤ`-linearity needs are not found.
  have h : ⇑(o.evalFundamentalClass hn M (ContinuousMap.id N)) =
      LinearMap.ringLmapEquivSelf ℤ ℕ M ∘ e.symm.arrowCongr (LinearEquiv.refl ℤ M) ∘
        ModuleCat.Hom.hom ∘ (TopCat.of N).singularKroneckerEquiv ℤ n := by
    ext c
    simp only [Function.comp_apply, LinearMap.ringLmapEquivSelf_apply,
      LinearEquiv.arrowCongr_apply, LinearEquiv.symm_symm, LinearEquiv.refl_apply, he,
      TopCat.singularKroneckerEquiv_apply, evalFundamentalClass_apply]
  rw [h]
  exact (LinearEquiv.bijective _).comp ((LinearEquiv.bijective _).comp
    (ModuleCat.hom_bijective.comp ((TopCat.of N).singularKroneckerEquiv ℤ n).bijective))

section UnitCoefficients

open MonoidalCategory

/- Cohomology with chain coefficients the unit object `ℤ` of `ModuleCat ℤ`, as in the cup pairing
`TopCat.singularCupPairing`, is taken with the `ℤ`-linear structure `ModuleCat.instLinear` of a
category of modules; instance search would otherwise find the structure
`Linear.preadditiveIntLinear` of a preadditive category, which `evalFundamentalClass` carries. -/
attribute [local instance 1100] ModuleCat.instLinear

/-- **Evaluation on `f_*[N]` with chain coefficients `ℤ`**: for an integral class `c ∈ Hⁿ(X; ℤ)`
with chain coefficients `ℤ`, evaluating its image under the coefficient isomorphism
`TauCeti.uliftIntIso` on `f_*[N]` is the Kronecker pairing of `c` with `f_*[N]` read with chain
coefficients `ℤ`. The two sides use the `ℤ`-linear structures of a preadditive category and of a
category of modules, which agree (`TopCat.singularKronecker_eqToHom`). -/
theorem evalFundamentalClass_singularCohomologyChainCoefficientMap_eq_singularKronecker
    (f : C(N, X))
    (c : (TopCat.of X).singularCohomology (𝟙_ (ModuleCat.{0} ℤ)) ℤ (ModuleCat.of ℤ ℤ) n) :
    o.evalFundamentalClass hn (ModuleCat.of ℤ ℤ) f
        ((TopCat.of X).singularCohomologyChainCoefficientMap ℤ (ModuleCat.of ℤ ℤ) uliftIntIso.hom n
          c) =
      ((TopCat.of X).singularKronecker ℤ n c).hom
        ((((singularHomologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{0} ℤ) n).map uliftIntIso.hom).app
          (TopCat.of X)).hom (o.mapFundamentalClass hn f)) := by
  have h := TopCat.singularKronecker_eqToHom (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) (ModuleCat.of ℤ ℤ)
    ModuleCat.instLinear Linear.preadditiveIntLinear (Subsingleton.elim _ _) (TopCat.of X) n
    ((TopCat.of X).singularCohomologyChainCoefficientMap ℤ (ModuleCat.of ℤ ℤ) uliftIntIso.hom n c)
  rw [TopCat.singularKronecker_singularCohomologyChainCoefficientMap] at h
  exact ConcreteCategory.congr_hom h (o.mapFundamentalClass hn f)

end UnitCoefficients

section Degree

variable {P G : Type} [TopologicalSpace P] [T2Space P]
  [NormedAddCommGroup G] [NormedSpace ℝ G] [FiniteDimensional ℝ G] [ChartedSpace G P]
  [CompactSpace P] [PreconnectedSpace P] (o' : HomologicalOrientation P G n)
  (hG : finrank ℝ G = n)

include hG in
/-- **The degree formula for the pairing**: for a map `f : N → P` of compact oriented
`n`-manifolds with `P` preconnected and any continuous `g : P → X`,
`⟨c, (g ∘ f)_*[N]⟩ = deg f • ⟨c, g_*[P]⟩`. -/
theorem evalFundamentalClass_comp_eq_degree_smul (g : C(P, X)) (f : C(N, P))
    (c : (TopCat.of X).singularCohomology (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) ℤ M n) :
    o.evalFundamentalClass hn M (g.comp f) c =
      o.degree o' hn f • o'.evalFundamentalClass hG M g c := by
  rw [evalFundamentalClass_apply, evalFundamentalClass_apply,
    o.mapFundamentalClass_comp_eq_degree_smul o' hn hG, map_zsmul]

include hG in
/-- **The degree formula for characteristic numbers**: for a map `f : N → P` of compact oriented
`n`-manifolds with `P` preconnected, evaluating the pull-back of `c ∈ Hⁿ(P; M)` on `[N]` is the
degree of `f` times evaluating `c` on `[P]`: `⟨f^* c, [N]⟩ = deg f • ⟨c, [P]⟩`. -/
theorem evalFundamentalClass_id_singularCohomologyMap_eq_degree_smul (f : C(N, P))
    (c : (TopCat.of P).singularCohomology (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) ℤ M n) :
    o.evalFundamentalClass hn M (ContinuousMap.id N)
        (TopCat.singularCohomologyMap (TopCat.ofHom f) n c) =
      o.degree o' hn f • o'.evalFundamentalClass hG M (ContinuousMap.id P) c := by
  rw [evalFundamentalClass_id_singularCohomologyMap, ← ContinuousMap.id_comp f,
    o.evalFundamentalClass_comp_eq_degree_smul hn M o' hG, ContinuousMap.id_comp]

end Degree

end HomologicalOrientation

end TauCeti
